{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "7aeb2189-969f-4edf-90d4-6d9e41ef1120"/*MeshToSDFExample*/,
  "Description": "How to bake a mesh into a raymarchable SDF volume with [MeshToSDF].\n\nA [CubeMesh] is converted into a distance field volume, which is then rendered with [RaymarchField]. Because the volume is baked, the mesh can be combined with procedural SDF primitives afterwards - see [CombineSDF], [BendField] or [PolarRepeat].\n\nTry changing Mode, Resolution and Smoothing on [MeshToSDF]: Jump Flood is the fast default, Exact Closest Point Scatter gives the smoothest surfaces near the mesh. [BakeProgress] and [BakeInProgress] show the bake while it is spread over frames; [BakeCount] increments when it completes.",
  "InputUis": [],
